# mv(1)

## NAME

mv - move or rename files

## SYNOPSIS

    mv source dest
    mv source... directory

## DESCRIPTION

Renames or moves files. If the destination is a directory, each source is moved into it. Moving to another file system copies the data and then removes the source.

## OPTIONS

- `-f`: accepted and ignored

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

## SEE ALSO

cp(1), rm(1)
